    "document_title": "VyomPath Golden Reference Traverses — Ground-Truth Elevation Fixtures",
    "version": "1.0",
    "date": "2026-10-26",
    "author": "Pranav Sharma (Terrain Lead, Team NAKSHATRA X)",
    "purpose": "Independent ground-truth elevation reference for unit tests. Each route provides verified elevation values for ≥5 sample points derived independently of terrain.py using raw rasterio pixel reads and pyproj transforms, matching the methods documented in unit_test_anchors.json.",
    "mars_radius_m": 3396190.0,
    "haversine_formula": "d = 2 * R * arcsin(sqrt(sin²(Δlat/2) + cos(lat1)·cos(lat2)·sin²(Δlon/2)))",
    "tolerance_mm": 1.0,
    "notes": [
      "J-gentle, J-steep, J-edge: elevation values sourced from tests/fixtures/demo_route_*_5m.json, generated by Shyam (GIS Lead) using gdallocationinfo + pyproj on jezero_aoi_v2.tif (Shyam local path: E:\\DATASETS\\_phase2\\jezero_aoi_v2.tif).",
      "S-basic: elevation values derived from data/dtm/syrtis_major_sample_dtm.tif via rasterio nearest-pixel read, using the file's own Equirectangular CRS (degree-unit coordinates, R=3396190 m, standard_parallel=0). No jezero_aoi_v2.tif required for S-basic tests.",
      "J-handcheck: A 6-point arithmetic-checkable route manually verified against unit_test_anchors.json anchor data (Sol-386 pixel col=1360, row=2157, elev=-2568.873 m).",
      "Tests using J-gentle, J-steep, J-edge, J-handcheck MUST be marked pytest.mark.skipif(not jezero_aoi_available, ...) since jezero_aoi_v2.tif is not present in CI."
    ]
  },
